From 9b0eb63fff26b523a7c5abb3155f76953b7a8737 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:41:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 31/42] bluetooth_audio: take the speakers from the server, and
 new ones at once

The add-on read the file of the paired devices once, when the media
services started: speakers paired afterwards became an output only after
a restart of the media services, and the file held the link keys of every
device for anyone to read.

It now asks bluetooth_server for the bonded devices (the new
BT_MSG_GET_BONDED_DEVICES, which gives no keys), and a small looper
watches the server's BT_NOTICE_BONDS_CHANGED and its start (the server
may start after the media services, and knows the bonds only once its
controller is set up; it now tells when it read them). Speakers that are
new then become an output at once, with NotifyFlavorChange(); a device
whose bond goes keeps its output until the media services restart, as
its node knows it by its index.

With nothing reading it any more, the server puts the old file aside as
Bluetooth_paired_devices.migrated, which only its owner may read.

Tested on the AC100: at boot the media server first stands in with the
sound card, and goes over to the Google Home as soon as the server has
read the bonds.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
